== 1. The collisions restated from their sources (Layer 3's table reproduced, then the cells on the pack)
Governing cell limits (MAKER, Samsung SDI INR18650-35E Ver. 1.1 (9 July 2015), v2/vendor/battery/samsung-35e-orbtronic.pdf): charge 0 to 45 C, discharge -10 to 60 C at the cell surface temperature; storage 1 month -20 to 60 C,
   3 months -20 to 45 C, 1 year -20 to 25 C, each at the ex-factory 30% of charge; the handling list: 'Don't leave, charge or use the battery in a car
   or similar place where inside of temperature may be over 60°C' (True) and 'Store the battery at temperature below 60°C' (True).
Version 1.0 (MAKER, Samsung SDI INR18650-35E Version No. 1.0, v2/vendor/battery/samsung-35e-akkuzentrum.pdf): charge 0 to 45 C and discharge -10 to 60 C (ambient); storage 1 year 0 to 23 C, 3 months 0 to 45 C, 1 month 0 to 60 C.
Heat inside (MODELED, PLAN): the heat stage after BANK-R1 (PS-SURV-R) 23.27 W plus the cells' I2R 0.174 W on the pack; as generated (PS-SURV) 21.73 W plus 0.152 W.

LO-01a  in use, the envelope's +40 C, battery-powered, the heat stage (in-use: operate to specification; acceptance E3-A, E3-L)
   inside air (MODELED): lid closed 62.12 C on the independent bound's lowest conductance, lid open 59.22 C; on 32.53's 55.63 C closed, 47.82 C open
   Layer 3's +62.1 C reproduced (rounded down): True; gap against +60 C: 2.12 K (on the inside air)
   on the pack the cells sit above that air by their own I2R (MODELED, pwr_budget.cell_temp, the block's lowest film): 63.29 C, gap 3.29 K;
   on 32.53's lid-closed conductance 56.22 C (no collision). Against the hot stop's first step (H1 at a reading of +56.5 C): 6.79 K over on the bound.
LO-01b  in use, the envelope's -20 C once warm: inside air -6.84 C on the highest conductance (rise 13.16 K, PS-IDLE-SPEC lid open); cells -5.52 C: above the -10 C floor by 4.48 K (no collision)
LO-01c  charging in use: the 0 to 45 C window is reached at ambients of -17.8 to +34.6 C by state on the independent bound (MODELED, the records' ceilings); the charge is held off outside it (no collision)
LO-01d  D-02a's +55 C operating margin, 4 h (E3-O; qualification margin: no damage and recovery to specification, no shutdown)
   inside air in the heat stage lid open, both configurations (MODELED): 61.63 to 74.22 C; gap 1.63 to 14.22 K (Layer 3: 1.6 to 14.2 K; True); on the pack at the worst corner 75.39 C
LO-01e  E5: 10 cycles of 24 h at 95 % RH, 30 to 60 C, on an input with the kit logging (qualification margin, SC-03): the pack idle at the inside air,
   66.63 to 79.22 C (MODELED); gap at least 6.63 K (Layer 3: at least 6.63 K; True); the dwell's length at +60 C stated in TEST-PLAN: no
LO-01f  D-02a's +71 C storage, 24 h (E3-S), stored kit, pack fitted, every input unplugged: cells at the ambient; gap 11 K (Layer 3: 11 K; True)
LO-01g  D-02a's -33 C storage, 24 h (E4-S): gap 13 K on Ver. 1.1, 33 K on Version 1.0 (Layer 3: 13 K; 33 K; True)
LO-01h  storage inside the envelope (-20 to +45 C three months, -20 to +25 C a year): none on Ver. 1.1; on Version 1.0 20 K at the cold end and 2 K at the one-year top (True)
   Lid open at the same corner (1.22 W/K): the cells on the pack reach 60.39 C and, on shore, the inside air 60.49 C (the front end's loss counted): past +60 C as well (3a).
In-use (the envelope, operate to specification): LO-01a, LO-01b, LO-01c, LO-01h. Qualification margins (D-02a, SC-03; no damage and recovery): LO-01d, LO-01e, LO-01f, LO-01g.

== 2. THE FEASIBILITY SCREEN: every required charging, discharging, transport and storage condition (the owner's refinement of 2 October 2026)
Each row: ambient, duration, configuration and charge state (TEST-PLAN), the governing MAKER limit, the power for thermal control, the gap, the approaches judged, the result.
A rejection is kept only where physics or a bounded figure gives it; a route with a missing input is INCONCLUSIVE, with the input named.
C01 discharge in use at the hot edge, on the pack, lid closed (E3-L at +40 C)
   ambient +40 C (REQ-024); duration 4 h at the level (E3-L); configuration deployed closed-lid, the heat stage, pack fitted, discharging
   limit: discharge -10 to 60 C at the cell surface (35E Ver. 1.1 3.12); the +59 C abort
   power for thermal control: the pack
   gap: 3.29 K at the bound's worst corner (63.29 C); none on 32.53's conductance (56.22 C)
   - the heat is the kit's own, so moving it out works: the enclosure's conductance decides (3a: 1.666 W/K for the complete pass line)
   - the coupling to the skin (3b) lowers the cells only; the inside air's criteria stay the enclosure's
   - a path to the face plate: the block sits on the floor under board B and the plate above it, and the plate, the air's main exit, runs near that air (INFERRED from 32.53's split): no gain
   - a lower heat stage: its 23 W carries REQ-052's required set
   SCREEN: CREDIBLE, CONDITIONAL on T-H1 (3a)
C02 on shore at the hot edge, the pack idle at the inside air (E3-L's second half, E3-A's 2 h on shore, E5-A)
   ambient +40 C; duration E3-A 4 h on the pack then 2 h on shore; E5-A 10 cycles of 24 hours at 95 percent relative humidity, the cycle of E5 with its upper level at the use envelope's +40 C; configuration deployed, lid open (E3-A, E5-A) or closed (E3-L), pack fitted, idle
   limit: +60 C, the idle pack's limit as REQ-046's note and REQ-077 read it
   power for thermal control: the input
   gap: lid closed 2.12 K; lid open at the bound's lowest the air on shore reaches 60.49 C and the cells on the pack 60.39 C
   - as C01, with the front end's loss on shore counted (3a)
   - charge state: the pack's charge at E3-A's start is not stated by TEST-PLAN (a named missing input)
   SCREEN: CREDIBLE, CONDITIONAL on T-H1 (3a), both lid states
C03 E3-A's +25 C point, 4 h, three loaded modules on shore (D-02b's charge point)
   ambient +25 C; duration 4 h; configuration deployed, lid open, on shore, the stage C1 selects
   limit: +60 C; no charge start above T3 42 C
   power for thermal control: the input
   gap: none for the cells: C1 sheds on measured temperatures; whether a charge starts is recorded (the charge ceiling of three loaded modules lies below +25 C, LO-01c)
   - none needed
   SCREEN: NO GAP (recorded, not judged on charging)
C04 E3-L's lower levels (+20 C, +30 C)
   ambient +20 C, +30 C; duration 4 h each, on the pack then on shore; configuration deployed closed-lid, the reduced mode or its heat stage
   limit: +60 C; the SGP41's +55 C air
   power for thermal control: the pack, then the input
   gap: none at the bound's worst corner: +20 C the reduced mode, cells 52.04 C; +30 C the heat stage (C1 acted), cells 53.29 C
   - none needed
   - mapped: E3-L is started once with the lid already closed, and the start with the lid closed enters the reduced mode once the lid is read; the levels' steady states above apply once the reduced mode runs (INFERRED: the start is shorter than the 4 h level)
   - charge state: the pack's charge at each level's start is not stated by TEST-PLAN (a named missing input)
   SCREEN: NO GAP
C05 E3-H's stepped run beyond the envelope (a protection test)
   ambient from +40 C by 2 K an hour to at most +55 C; duration until H1 and then H2 have acted; configuration lid closed, the heat stage, pack fitted, on shore then on the pack
   limit: no cell at +59 C before H1 and H2 act; no permanent protection
   power for thermal control: the input, then the pack
   gap: none for the cells: past H2 the kit's heat stops and the cells approach the chamber's at most +55 C (quasi-static at 2 K an hour against time constants of hours, INFERRED); whether H2 is reached depends on the minimum load's heat, not modelled (P15 forces it)
   - the hot stop itself
   - mapped: at +40 C lid closed the level is held until the hot stop has acted or its 4 h have passed; the run is repeated with the sensor controller held in reset, when board B's TMP117 acts at +55.0 C (shed) and +56.0 C (shutdown), released at +45.0 C
   - restart: the heat stage's module returns once the hottest cell reads +46.5 C or less and 30 minutes have passed; after H2 MAIN restarts it with no module raised above +46.5 C
   - charge state: not stated by TEST-PLAN for E3-H (a named missing input; the thermal figures do not depend on it, the run's energy does)
   SCREEN: NO GAP for the cells; a step not reached reads NOT_VERIFIED (TEST-PLAN)
C06 discharge in use at the cold edge, once warm (E4-O)
   ambient -20 C; duration 4 h; configuration deployed, pack fitted, heater active, started warm or on an input
   limit: discharge floor -10 C
   power for thermal control: the pack, or the input
   gap: none: cells -5.52 C on the highest conductance
   - none needed
   SCREEN: NO GAP
C07 a start from a pack cold-soaked below about -10 C
   ambient below about -10 C at the cells; duration the start; configuration pack fitted
   limit: discharge floor -10 C
   power for thermal control: shore or vehicle input, or warming
   gap: out of scope by the owner's D-02d
   - no requirement: D-02d
   SCREEN: NOT REQUIRED (D-02d)
C08 charging in use, hot
   ambient -20 to +40 C; duration a mission; configuration deployed, pack fitted, charging
   limit: charge 0 to 45 C at the cell surface; T3 42 C
   power for thermal control: the input
   gap: none by requirement: held off outside the window (reached at -17.8 to +34.6 C ambient)
   - none needed; D-02b's accepted consequence
   SCREEN: NO GAP
C09 charging in use, cold (the mat before charge, REQ-046)
   ambient -20 C; duration the warm-up, then the charge; configuration deployed, pack fitted, on an input
   limit: charge from 0 C; UTC 1.0 C, the panel's +3 C hold
   power for thermal control: the input (the mat 7.5 W into the cells, 1.0 W regulator loss into the air)
   gap: the mat lifts the idle cells to 12.44 C
   - powered heating with a source present and the existing hold-then-warm start; its use is on the input
   SCREEN: CREDIBLE: the existing mat (3d)
C10 D-02a's +55 C operating margin (E3-O)
   ambient +55 C; duration 4 h; configuration deployed, monitor and radios on, on shore or vehicle input, pack fitted (FEA-008)
   limit: +60 C (surface and the idle pack); H1 at a reading of +56.5 C; E3-O's 'no shutdown'
   power for thermal control: the input
   gap: 1.63 to 14.22 K
   - fans and heat spreading cannot cool the cells below a hotter ambient; the cells may sit 5 K over +55 C against a 6.63 to 19.22 K rise
   - insulation: no hold over 14400 s (time constant 1081 to 4457 s), and in steady state 6.7 to 13.7 mm at k 0.02 W/mK against 0.77 to 2.66 mm: rejected
   - the coupling: the cells pass H1's reading at every corner (59.10 C at the best): the hot stop stops every module: rejected
   - added latent storage (3n): under +60 C it fits only at the best corner; the complete pass is rejected by the 0.79 K window under H1 against a 3 K melting area
   - powered cooling on the input: cold side 0.76 to 7.87 W; rejected into the sealed case at the worst corner, INCONCLUSIVE at the conditioned corner (the air lifted onto the +70 C parts) and near the best (3i, 3o)
   - (II) a wide-temperature cell with the protection re-derived: CONDITIONAL, the cells 6.93 K under the re-derived H1's no-act limit at the conditioned corner (4d)
   - charge state: the pack's charge in E3-O is not stated by TEST-PLAN (a named missing input)
   SCREEN: OPEN: (II) recommended, CONDITIONAL; passive design and latent storage rejected; cooling INCONCLUSIVE with its cost to other parts
C11 E5's humid cycle (SC-03 margin)
   ambient 30 to 60 C at 95 % RH; duration 10 cycles of 24 h (Method 507.6 Procedure II, mapped in 3n); configuration deployed, logging, on shore or vehicle input, pack fitted (FEA-008)
   limit: +60 C
   power for thermal control: the input
   gap: at least 6.63 K at the +60 C dwell
   - fans and heat spreading cannot cool the cells below a hotter ambient
   - the profile mapped from Method 507.6 Procedure II (3n): a 23 C conditioning, ten 24 h cycles 30-60-60-30-30 C, a return to 23 C; operational checks near the ends of the fifth and tenth cycles
   - added latent storage over that profile (3n, 3o): a marginal fit at the best corner, none at the conditioned and the worst: INCONCLUSIVE
   - powered cooling: cold side 1.50 to 10.09 W; rejected into the sealed case at the worst corner, INCONCLUSIVE at the conditioned corner (the air lifted onto the +70 C parts) and near the best (3i, 3o)
   - (II) a wide-temperature cell: CONDITIONAL, the cells 1.06 K under the re-derived H1's no-act limit at the conditioned corner (4d)
   - charge state: the pack's charge in E5 is not stated by TEST-PLAN (a named missing input)
   SCREEN: OPEN: (II) recommended, CONDITIONAL; latent storage and cooling INCONCLUSIVE with their limits named
C12 D-02a's +71 C storage margin (E3-S)
   ambient +71 C; duration 24 h; configuration stored: closed, latched, every input unplugged, pack fitted at 30% of charge in its gauge's shutdown (REQ-025, SC-19)
   limit: storage 1 month -20 to 60 C at 30% of charge (35E Ver. 1.1 3.13)
   power for thermal control: zero from the inputs and the stored pack (its FETs off); a separate source only if one is added
   gap: 11 K: the ambient alone exceeds the limit
   - fans and spreading: no power and no colder sink
   - the calculated insulation for the 24 h: 24.6 mm needed against 2.66 mm (3f): rejected
   - added latent storage (3n): 0.275 to 1.175 L needed against the pocket's 0.056 to 0.121 L: rejected within the pocket
   - powered cooling from a second energy store: added storage under D-06, INCONCLUSIVE (3i)
   - (II) a wide-temperature cell: CONDITIONAL, 9.00 K under the page's +80 C storage row, U2 moved to BQ7720704 (4d)
   SCREEN: OPEN: (II) recommended, CONDITIONAL; zero-power design and latent storage rejected within the pocket
C13 D-02a's -33 C storage margin (E4-S)
   ambient -33 C; duration 24 h; configuration stored, as C12
   limit: storage floor -20 C (Ver. 1.1); 0 C (Version 1.0); discharge floor -10 C
   power for thermal control: zero from the inputs and the stored pack; a separate primary source only if one is added
   gap: 13 K (Ver. 1.1); 33 K (Version 1.0)
   - the calculated insulation: 30.3 mm needed (3f): rejected
   - added latent storage: no maker's sheet of a material freezing between -20 and -10 C is held: INCONCLUSIVE
   - a heater fed by the pack (case i): the discharge window applies and its FETs are off in shutdown (3g): rejected within REQ-025; its 1.3 to 8.6 h are model sensitivities, not the basis
   - a heater fed by a primary battery (case i), bounded in 3n: added energy storage under D-06, not adopted: INCONCLUSIVE
   - a pack already cold-soaked (case ii): not recovered by any heater below -20 C; the pack cannot feed one below -10 C
   - heating lost (case iii): past the floor 0.30 to 1.09 h after a pack-fed hold, at once for a hold at the floor (3g)
   - (II) a wide-temperature cell: CONDITIONAL, 7.00 K inside the page's -40 C storage row, no heater and no store (4d)
   SCREEN: OPEN: (II) recommended, CONDITIONAL; the pack-fed heater rejected; the primary a proposal under D-06
C14 storage inside the envelope
   ambient -20 to +45 C; -20 to +25 C; duration three months; a year; configuration stored, as C12
