   - none needed
   SCREEN: NO GAP
C16 E4-T, the stored and transport cold soak
   ambient the lowest storage temperature of the governing cell specification, 24 h; duration 24 h; configuration closed, latched, kit off, pack fitted in shutdown
   limit: storage floor -20 C (Ver. 1.1) at 30% of charge; F2's operating floor -20 C
   power for thermal control: zero
   gap: none for the cells at the ex-factory state; F2's storage line (-10 C) open with Eaton
   - none needed
   - recovery mapped: full function after return to 25 C, capacity within 5 % of its value before (PROVISIONAL: the maker publishes no cold-storage recovery figure)
   - charge state: the ex-factory state for storage; for transport 'at its charge', not stated (a named missing input)
   SCREEN: NO GAP for the cells
C17 E3-P, the pack alone, armed, at full charge, then discharged from +58 C
   ambient +58 C set point, +-2 K; duration 24 h, then a 2 A discharge until the gauge stops it; configuration the pack alone, JP1 closed, full charge
   limit: at full charge the maker's 20 days at 60 C (MAKER 7.10); discharge to 60 C; F2 60 C
   power for thermal control: the pack (the test load)
   gap: none by construction: the soak sits at the limits; the pass line asks OTD (57.5 C in the reading) to stop the discharge before any cell exceeds +60 C and to recover at or below +52.5 C; whether it acts at once depends on the reading's error, so no immediate refusal is claimed
   - none needed
   SCREEN: NO GAP (a protection test at the limits)
C18 E4-P, the pack alone at its cold storage limit
   ambient as E4-T (the lowest storage temperature of the governing cell specification, 24 h); duration 24 h; configuration the pack alone (as E4-T)
   limit: storage floor -20 C at 30% of charge; no cold-storage recovery figure published (PROVISIONAL pass line)
   power for thermal control: zero
   gap: none for the cells at the ex-factory state; another charge state is not in the sheet
   - none needed
   - recovery mapped (as E4-T): full function after return to 25 C, capacity within 5 % of its value before (PROVISIONAL: the maker publishes no cold-storage recovery figure)
   - charge state: E4-P names none (a named missing input); the sheet's storage rows hold at the ex-factory 30 %
   SCREEN: NO GAP at the ex-factory state
C19 P13, F2 at temperature: 18 A for 60 s from +55 C, and 10 A for 1 h at the pack's hot limit
   ambient +55 C block; the pack's hot limit; duration 60 s; 1 h; configuration a block on the bench, a thermocouple on F2's body
   limit: +60 C at the cells and at F2's body
   power for thermal control: the test load
   gap: the key-down: none for the cells (56.37 to 58.24 C); the hour: the cells' own 4.67 to 8.00 W rise them 10.5 to 54.0 K over the block's air, so 'at the hot limit' must mean the cell surface (3k)
   - a definition item for P13's owner; F2's body is the measurement
   SCREEN: NO GAP for the cells if the limit is held at the cell surface; F2 open

== 3. The thermal routes, bounded
3a LO-01a: the thresholds (MODELED, PS-SURV-R at PLAN heat, +40 C; on shore the front end's and charger's loss on the loads adds 1.725 W; the block's lowest film).
   The conductance from which each criterion holds (W/K), the same in either lid state:
   cell rating (+60 C)                                            on the pack  1.2455
   the +59 C abort (FEA-008 LO-01a)                               on the pack  1.3154
   H1 not acting (reading under +56.5 C, no sensor allowance)     on the pack  1.5300
   H1 not acting with the 0.71 K reading-high term                on the pack  1.6043
   SGP41 inside air at most +55 C                                 on the pack  1.5630
   F2 at the inside air at most +60 C                             on the pack  1.1723
   cell rating (+60 C)                                            on the shore 1.2498
   the +59 C abort (FEA-008 LO-01a)                               on the shore 1.3156
   H1 not acting (reading under +56.5 C, no sensor allowance)     on the shore 1.5149
   H1 not acting with the 0.71 K reading-high term                on the shore 1.5831
   SGP41 inside air at most +55 C                                 on the shore 1.6664
   F2 at the inside air at most +60 C                             on the shore 1.2498
   The cell rating alone: 1.2455 W/K on the pack. FEA-008's own LO-01a criterion (the +59 C abort): 1.3154 W/K. The complete E3-A and E3-L pass line: 1.6664 W/K (SGP41 inside air at most +55 C, on shore).
   T-H1 must read at least 1.666 W/K with the fans, lid closed AND lid open (the heat stage runs in both). The record's bounds: independent 1.06 to 2.49 (closed) and 1.22 to 2.85 W/K (open);
   appendix 32.53 1.5 to 2.0 (closed) and 3.0 to 3.3 W/K (open). Lid open at the bound's lowest 1.22 W/K the cells on the pack reach 60.39 C and the air on shore 60.49 C: past +60 C as well.
   Dependencies that fail today and stay visible: On board B as generated the stage criteria fail at any level where the heat stage is entered, because its one-module stage lacks the LoRa mesh and APRS (TEST-PLAN E3-L); F2's body (P13, PWR-F12); the gauge's ADC and gradient terms (P14, not in the thresholds above); HIGH heat (not covered).
3b The pocket coupling measure: the block's east face (0.00509 m2) against the east wall through a gap filler of the pocket's widest gap (9.68 mm, CASE-MARGINS M4b; k 1.0 W/mK, ASSUMPTION),
   its base (0.00756 m2) on the floor through the heater mat (1.5 mm, k 0.2 W/mK, ASSUMPTION; the mat's sheet states neither: True); the other four faces (0.01697 m2) in the inside air at 5.0 to 15.0 W/m2K.
   Coupling to ambient 0.0544 (worst) to 0.0901 W/K (best), to the inside air 0.2545 (worst) to 0.0848 W/K (best): f = 0.824 to 0.485; the enclosure loses 0.0377 to 0.0735 W/K of skin (counted); a 3 W/mK filler adds 0.0015 W/K.
   LO-01a lid closed at the bound's lowest: cells 63.29 C without it (two-node reproduces pwr_budget: True), 58.64 C (worst) to 51.99 C (best) with it; on shore 59.30 C. Against the complete pass line:
      cell rating    58.64 C against 60.00 C: holds
      the +59 C abort 58.64 C against 59.00 C: holds
      H1 reading     58.64 C against 56.50 C: fails by 2.14 K
      SGP41 air      61.94 C against 55.00 C: fails by 6.94 K
      F2 at the air  61.94 C against 60.00 C: fails by 1.94 K
   So the measure meets the cell criteria on the pack only: on shore the cells reach 59.30 C, past the +59 C abort, and the air 63.42 C (check 2). The air criteria stay the
   enclosure's (3a). It is a partial fallback for the cells, never a substitute for T-H1's conductance.
   Placement: the block's top lies about 3.66 mm under board B's underside (SHORTLIST's 2.66 mm of room plus the 1.0 mm minimum, CASE-MARGINS M6), which has no local model (POWER-THERMAL.md 9.2).
3c The cold end the measure touches (LO-01b; PS-IDLE-SPEC on the pack, lid open, -20 C, the highest conductance): cells -5.52 C without it, -10.24 C with it (-9.22 C on W4's highest);
   holding -8.0 C (1 K over UTD's -9.0 C reading, INFERRED) takes 0.38 W into the cells, 0.44 W from the battery with the mat's regulator (1.0 % of PS-IDLE-SPEC's 42.82 W; firmware owner).
3d Charging at the cold end: the mat puts 7.5 W into the block (MAKER, RS PRO 245-556 at 12 V) and its regulator 1.0 W into the air (POWER-THERMAL.md 7.1); at -20 C on input power, the pack idle,
   the cells reach 12.44 C (record's model) and 12.84 C (with the coupling): over UTC's 1.0 C and the panel's +3 C hold (MODELED).
3e Storage hold times (INFERRED): the cells' own time constant in the pocket 1081 to 4457 s; the closed, stopped kit 1.53 to 3.97 h (32.53's 8 to 10 kJ/K over the lid-closed still-air bound).
   After 24 h from the most favourable start (steps of 91 K and 78 K) the cells lag the ambient by 0.21 K (hot) and 0.18 K (cold) as one node, 0.351 K and 0.301 K as two nodes
   (the kit's 9340 J/K beside the cells' 660 J/K, 0.70 W/K to ambient, 0.1481 W/K to the cells). Heating the whole kit at the -20 C floor for 24 h would take 218 to 452 Wh (the first issue's figure);
   heating only the pack is 3g.
3f LO-01f passive: to keep the cells within 80 K of the start for 24 h against a 91 K step (two nodes, the slowest kit), the pack's coupling must fall under 0.0207 W/K from 0.1481:
   24.6 mm of insulation at k 0.02 W/mK (ASSUMPTION) round the block with the cells' own heat capacity, against 0.77 to 2.66 mm of room: that arrangement is rejected (today 90.65 K); added storage is 3n.
3f LO-01g passive: to keep the cells within 65 K of the start for 24 h against a 78 K step (two nodes, the slowest kit), the pack's coupling must fall under 0.0173 W/K from 0.1481:
   30.3 mm of insulation at k 0.02 W/mK (ASSUMPTION) round the block with the cells' own heat capacity, against 0.77 to 2.66 mm of room: that arrangement is rejected (today 77.70 K); added storage is 3n.
3g LO-01g, the -33 C storage margin (E4-S, 24 h), in three cases. Ambient and cell temperatures are kept apart; the pack's discharge window (-10 to +60 C, 3.12) governs
   whenever the pack feeds a heater, the storage rows only when it does not. One boundary: the source's terminals; the mat's 7.5 W into the block, its regulator's 0.133 of that into the air,
   the gauge's NORMAL draw (336 uA typical, MAKER SLUSC67B 6.5: 0.0048 W) when the pack feeds it. Slow and fast corners: 0.1222 and 0.3400 W/K in series (pack, air, case).
   WITHDRAWN as a feasibility basis: the comparison of 38.1 to 106.1 Wh with the pack's nominal 144.7 Wh. It is a nominal comparison; the usable-energy comparison below replaces it.
   (i) A warm pack kept inside its limits for the exposure.
      Fed by the pack: the heater discharges the cells, so the setpoint is UTD's -9.0 C reading plus the published cold-side budget 0.86 K = -8.14 C (the gradient and ADC terms TBD).
      Hold: 2.97 to 8.20 W into the cells, 3.37 to 9.30 W at the pack's terminals, 80.9 to 223.1 Wh for 24 h with no cool-down credit.
      At the fast corner the 8.20 W into the cells exceeds the mat's own 7.5 W at 12 V (MAKER): a further inability of the present mat to hold that setpoint.
      MODEL SENSITIVITY, not usable energy: 30 % of charge (Ver. 1.1 3.13) less the 5 % reserve, aged to 80 % (SC-23), at the nominal voltage, times a cold factor between 0.41 and 1.0
      gives 11.9 to 28.9 Wh, 1.3 to 8.6 h of the 24 h, a balance of -211.2 to -51.9 Wh; from a full charge 4.9 to 32.6 h. MAKER 7.5's point is a full standard charge, a 3 h
      temperature change and 3.4 A to 2.65 V; it does not give this regime. Missing: the terminal energy over the partial-charge voltage curve, the cutoff, the temperature history.
      The rejection does not rest on these figures: in the stored state the gauge is in shutdown, 'In SHUTDOWN mode, the device turns off the FETs after FET Off Time' (MAKER, SLUUAQ3A 5.4.2), so the pack-fed heater
      has no protected path unless the gauge stays awake, a change of REQ-025's stored state.
      Scope: not available at REQ-025's stored state (its shutdown); the durations above are sensitivities, not a basis either way.
      Fed by a separate primary source (the pack stays in its storage row and in shutdown): setpoint the -20 C floor plus the thermostat's tolerance and the in-pack gradient (both TBD):
      1.59 to 4.42 W into the cells at the floor itself, 38.1 to 106.1 Wh for 24 h driven direct (42.2 to 116.6 Wh through the 12 V regulator), plus 2.93 to 8.16 Wh per K of margin.
      Start and control: a thermostat on the block, independent of the gauge and the kit (both off), arms with the stored state and closes at its setpoint; the source must deliver at -33 C.
      Its usable energy at -33 C, the thermostat's tolerance, the gradient, a place in the case and its transport classification (D-04) are NAMED UNKNOWNS: its duration is not computed.
      Cool-down credit (ASSUMPTION: E4-S's starting state is not stated; from the sheet's 23 C standard temperature): 1.57 to 4.57 h before the pack reaches -8.14 C, 2.58 to 7.27 h before -20 C.
      Recovery: E4-O follows E4-S (4 h at -20 C); a pack held at the -20 C floor is below the -10 C discharge floor, so E4-O starts from shore or vehicle input or after
      warming, as TEST-PLAN and D-02d already allow; a pack held at -8.14 C could start from itself.
   (ii) A pack already cold-soaked before any heater starts: below -20 C it has already left its storage row and no heater undoes that; between -20 and -10 C the pack may not
      discharge (3.12) and the gauge holds its discharge FET off below UTD (recovery -4.0 C), so only a separate source can rewarm it: 0.133 to 0.183 Wh into the cells per K, plus the losses.
      Its scope if the unknowns land: E4-S's 24 h at -33 C from a warm stored kit, the source supplying at least 38.1 to 106.1 Wh at -33 C plus 2.93 to 8.16 Wh per K of margin and its own reserve.
      F2 sits at about the inside air (-30.7 to -30.0 C at the hold), below its -20 C operating floor: Eaton's answer, or the heated zone extended to board P (a Layer 7 item).
   (iii) Heating lost, or its energy spent, at the pack-fed hold: the cells pass the -20 C floor 0.30 to 1.09 h later (two nodes, from the heated steady state); a separately fed
      hold at the floor itself passes it at once, so its margin must cover the source's depletion as well. Neither the gauge (in shutdown) nor the kit records the event (a named item).
3h E5's cycle: TEST-PLAN states 10 cycles of 24 h between 30 and 60 C and no dwell or ramp. Any passive network passes the cycle's mean, so the pack's surroundings average
   the mean ambient plus the rise: storage can help only if the mean ambient is under 40.78 C (worst rise) to 53.37 C (best). For a symmetric cycle (mean 45 C, 15 K amplitude, ASSUMPTION):
   possible at the worst corner: no; at the best a 5.68 h time constant, regeneration in the cool half included, so 14.4 to 21.2 mm of insulation or 3.0 to 9.1 kJ/K of added heat capacity,
   against 0.77 to 2.66 mm and a full pocket: INCONCLUSIVE until the profile is stated; for the symmetric profile, not within D-06's pocket.
3i Powered cooling (a thermoelectric stage; COP 0.5 to 1.0 ASSUMPTION, no module's sheet held). Corrected balance (check 2): heat pumped out of the block into the inside air returns to
   the air it came from, so the air gains only the cooler's input Q_c/COP: G_e a = q + G_b (a - d)/COP, an equilibrium wherever G_e > G_b/COP.
   E3-O  hold 56.50 C, into the inside air: best COP 0.5: air 62.6 C, load 0.91 W, input 1.81 W; best COP 1.0: air 62.3 C, load 0.86 W, input 0.86 W; worst COP 0.5: air 126.4 C, load 31.04 W, input 62.08 W; worst COP 1.0: air 86.4 C, load 13.27 W, input 13.27 W
   E5    hold 56.50 C, into the inside air: best COP 0.5: air 68.1 C, load 1.72 W, input 3.44 W; best COP 1.0: air 67.6 C, load 1.64 W, input 1.64 W; worst COP 0.5: air 144.8 C, load 39.21 W, input 78.42 W; worst COP 1.0: air 94.2 C, load 16.76 W, input 16.76 W
   E3-S  hold 57.93 C, into the inside air: best COP 0.5: air 74.4 C, load 2.43 W, input 4.86 W; best COP 1.0: air 72.5 C, load 2.16 W, input 2.16 W; worst COP 0.5: no equilibrium; worst COP 1.0: air 93.7 C, load 15.89 W, input 15.89 W
   So, into the sealed case: at the worst corners of E3-O and E5 the air reaches 86.4 to 144.8 C at COP 0.5 to 1.0, past every part limit of OPERATING-ENVELOPE.md section 2
   (F2 +60 C, the SGP41 +55 C); at their best corners the cells can be held for 0.86 to 3.44 W of input with the air 0.70 to 1.48 K above its uncooled value (which already passes F2
   and the SGP41 on its own).
   E3-O  with the air unchanged (heat sent out of the case): load 0.76 to 7.87 W; a path out needs 0.051 to 0.525 W/K (COP 1.0), 0.076 to 0.787 W/K (COP 0.5), hot side at most 30 K over the chamber
   E5    with the air unchanged (heat sent out of the case): load 1.50 to 10.09 W; a path out needs 0.100 to 0.673 W/K (COP 1.0), 0.150 to 1.009 W/K (COP 0.5), hot side at most 30 K over the chamber
   E3-S  with the air unchanged (heat sent out of the case): load 1.60 to 4.44 W; a path out needs 0.106 to 0.296 W/K (COP 1.0), 0.160 to 0.444 W/K (COP 0.5), hot side at most 30 K over the chamber
   The pack's own skin path (3b) is 0.054 to 0.090 W/K: enough only at E3-O's best corner. E3-S has no input: 38 to 213 Wh over 24 h from a separate source.
   Result: rejected into the sealed case at the worst corners for COP up to 1.0; at the best corners and for a higher COP INCONCLUSIVE, the inputs missing: a cooler's maker
   sheet (load against lift, COP), the input's spare power (L4-E4's 4.70 A limit less the kit's load, not derived here), the volume (a module and its spreader in a 6.38 mm gap).
3j PWR-F12's key-down: 18 A for 60 s (6.0 A a cell) from C1's +55 C warms the cells 1.37 to 3.24 K adiabatically (MODELED), to 56.37 to 58.24 C, inside +60 C.
3k P13's hour at 10 A (3.33 A a cell): the cells' own 4.67 to 8.00 W, a steady rise of 10.5 to 54.0 K over the block's film and 25.5 to 60.0 K adiabatic over the hour (MODELED):
   'the block at the pack's hot limit' holds the cells inside +60 C only if the limit is set at the cell surface and the chamber runs that much cooler (a definition item for P13's owner).
3l E3-L's levels at the bound's lowest lid-closed conductance (MODELED): +20 C: the reduced mode, air 49.90 C, cells 52.04 C; +30 C: the heat stage (C1 acted), air 52.12 C, cells 53.29 C; +40 C: the heat stage (C1 acted), air 62.12 C, cells 63.29 C

3n The open rows' next bounded actions, from makers' documents and without a purchase (the final round).
   Room round the block beyond the 1.0 mm minimums (INFERRED, CASE-MARGINS and SHORTLIST): 0.056 L at the worst stack, 0.121 L as designed.
   Latent storage, MAKER (Rubitherm RT57HC, `v2/vendor/battery/pcm/`): melting area 55 to 58 C, 240 kJ/kg +-7.5 % (latent and sensible), cp 2000 J/kgK, 0.9 kg/l solid.
   Taken favourable to the material: 258 kJ/kg all latent at the top of its melting area (58 C), the solid density, no container, perfect contact with the cells.
   (b) E5: TEST-PLAN cites '507' with Procedure II's levels; MIL-STD-810H Method 507.6 (transcribed, `v2/vendor/standards/mil-std-810h-method-507-6.md`) gives a 23 C conditioning
      for at least 24 h, then 10 cycles of 0 h 30, 2 h 60, 8 h 60, 16 h 30, 24 h 30 (h, C), RH 95 %, then a return to 23 C until stable; the cycle's mean is 43.75 C. Which procedure E5 means is the plan owner's to confirm.
      best  corner (the heat stage on shore, lid open): air mean 50.82 C; without storage the cells peak at 66.72 C; they stay under +60 C with 0.092 kg (0.102 L)
      worst corner (the heat stage on shore, lid open): air mean 64.24 C; without storage the cells peak at 79.63 C; they stay under +60 C with 6.406 kg (7.118 L)
      So: at the best corner a marginal fit (between the worst-stack and the designed room); at the worst no fit. INCONCLUSIVE on the conductance and the built room.
   (c) LO-01d, E3-O's 4 h at +55 C from a kit stabilised at the chamber: without storage the cells peak at 61.26 C (best) and 72.42 C (worst); under +60 C with
      0.011 kg (0.012 L, inside the room) at the best corner and 0.183 kg (0.203 L, outside it) at the worst. The complete pass ('no shutdown') needs the cells under H1's no-act
      limit 55.79 C with the chamber already at 55 C: a 0.79 K window against the material's 55 to 58 C melting area. Rejected against the present hot-stop ladder.
   LO-01f, E3-S's 24 h at +71 C from the storage envelope's cold edge: under +60 C with 0.248 kg (0.275 L) at the best corner and 1.057 kg (1.175 L) at the worst: beyond the room.
   LO-01g: no maker's sheet of a material freezing between -20 and -10 C is held: INCONCLUSIVE.
   Each store's history (no fresh store is assumed): E3-O starts from the kit stabilised at +55 C with the material solid at the bottom of its melting area (favourable:
      its partial melting below 55 C is not counted); E5's store is carried through the conditioning and all 10 cycles in one run, refreezing only as the cycle's 30 C part
      allows; E3-S starts at the storage envelope's cold edge (favourable). Once the store is spent the cells follow the no-storage response: E3-O to 61.26 to 72.42 C, E5 to
      66.72 to 79.63 C, E3-S to 70.65 to 71.00 C. Between required exposures the store resets only below 55 C, which each test's own return to ambient provides; a kit taken from
      one hot exposure to the next without it starts with a spent store.
   (a) LO-01g's primary battery: ADDED ENERGY STORAGE, a proposal under D-06, bounded here and not adopted. MAKER (Saft LSH 20, Li-SOCl2, D size, Document 31015-2-0426,
      held back): 13 Ah under 14 mA at +20 C, 3.6 V, at most 1.8 A continuous,
      -60 to +85 C, 33.4 x 61.31 mm, 100 g, about 3.8 g of lithium, UN 3090 and UN 3091, self-discharge 'less than 3% per year of storage, at + 20°C, after 1 year'. Its curves are typical, not minimum (the maker's own words: True);
      read by eye (INFERRED, `inputs/saft-lsh20-curves-read-2026-10-01.json`) at -40 C and -20 C, interpolated in current and temperature.
      One boundary: the string drives the existing mat (19.2 ohm, MAKER 7.5 W at 12 V) through a thermostat, no regulator; the demand is the series path times the hold's rise.
      Setpoint: the -20 C floor plus thermostat 3.0 K + gradient 2.0 K + margin 2.0 K = 7.0 K (ASSUMPTION, no thermostat part held); reserve kept: typical against minimum 20 % + self-discharge over the replacement interval 6 % = 26 % (ASSUMPTION).
      4S, -40 C curve (lower)        568 mA on, 2.729 V a cell, 4.57 Ah, 6.2 W on, 49.8 Wh a string; slow corner: 2.44 W average (duty 0.39), 2 strings, 8 cells, 0.8 kg, 0.43 L, 30.2 h, balance 15.1 Wh;
                                     fast corner: 6.80 W average (duty 1.10, above 1: the mat's on-power cannot carry it), 5 strings, 20 cells, 2.0 kg, 1.07 L, 27.1 h, balance 21.2 Wh
      4S, at the hold's air          598 mA on, 2.873 V a cell, 5.03 Ah, 6.9 W on, 57.8 Wh a string; slow corner: 2.44 W average (duty 0.36), 2 strings, 8 cells, 0.8 kg, 0.43 L, 35.0 h, balance 26.9 Wh;
                                     fast corner: 6.80 W average (duty 0.99), 4 strings, 16 cells, 1.6 kg, 0.86 L, 25.2 h, balance 8.0 Wh
      5S, -40 C curve (lower)        704 mA on, 2.703 V a cell, 4.39 Ah, 9.5 W on, 59.3 Wh a string; slow corner: 2.44 W average (duty 0.26), 2 strings, 10 cells, 1.0 kg, 0.54 L, 35.9 h, balance 29.1 Wh;
                                     fast corner: 6.80 W average (duty 0.72), 4 strings, 20 cells, 2.0 kg, 1.07 L, 25.8 h, balance 12.4 Wh
      5S, at the hold's air          742 mA on, 2.850 V a cell, 4.82 Ah, 10.6 W on, 68.6 Wh a string; slow corner: 2.44 W average (duty 0.23), 2 strings, 10 cells, 1.0 kg, 0.54 L, 41.6 h, balance 42.9 Wh;
                                     fast corner: 6.80 W average (duty 0.64), 4 strings, 20 cells, 2.0 kg, 1.07 L, 29.9 h, balance 39.9 Wh
      Bound: 5S on the -40 C curve (4S's on-power falls under the fast corner's demand). 10 to 20 cells, 1.0 to 2.0 kg, 0.54 to 1.07 L of cells, 25.8 to 35.9 h with the reserve kept.
      Fit: the cells alone exceed the pocket's 0.121 L, so they sit elsewhere in the case: Layer 7's free volume is the missing fact. F2 sits at about -30 C, below its -20 C floor:
      a separate obstacle (Eaton, or the heated zone over board P). Sequence: the pack to its ex-factory charge and the gauge to shutdown (REQ-025); the storage heater armed; its
      thermostat on the coldest cell closes at the setpoint and connects the string to the mat, isolated from the kit's 12 V feed (a circuit item for the generator owners); the
      pack never discharges; disarmed at the end of storage. Scope: E4-S's 24 h at -33 C from a warm stored kit; not a cold start, not in use.
      Against D-06: 10 to 20 cells hold 470 to 940 Wh nominal (MAKER, 47 Wh a cell), 3.2 to 6.5 times the pack's 144.7 Wh, and 38 to 76 g of lithium: a second energy
      store beside D-06's one pack. Calling it a heater supply does not settle its compatibility with D-06 (one 4S3P pack, internal storage, no external battery): adopting it is the owner's.
      Bounded per measure (MAKER where quoted): output at the cold load from the typical curves above; startup: the pulse figures hold 'after initial stabilisation' (True) and no
      figure is given at -33 C after storage (missing); ageing: under 3 % a year at +20 C, its typical values 'relative to cells stored up to one year at + 30°C max' (True), the
      recommended storage at most +30 C against the kit's envelope to +45 C, E3-T's +58 C and E3-S's +71 C, so its energy after storage in the kit is unsupported (Saft's answer
      missing); replacement as a set ('Do not mix new and used cells': True) every 2 years (ASSUMPTION); unintended charging: 'Do not recharge' (True), so the string reaches the
      mat only through a blocking path the kit's 12 V feed cannot back-drive (two series diodes, a circuit draft, no standard held); fit: outside the pocket (above).
      The three cases: (i) keeping a warm pack is its job; (ii) a pack already cold-soaked is rewarmed only from this store, 0.133 to 0.183 Wh per K (3g); (iii) lost control:
      with the store spent or the thermostat failed open the cells pass -20 C 0.30 to 1.09 h later (3g); failed closed, the mat runs at 9.5 W, the cells settle at -5.0 to 44.8 C
      (inside their storage row) and the store is spent in 12.5 to 24.9 h.
3o The conditioned corner. Every approach carries LO-01a's condition, T-H1 reading at least 1.666 W/K in each lid state; with the kit's conductance at that floor and every
   other parameter at its worst (the heat stage on shore, the lowest heat capacities, the fastest block), on the same profiles as 3n: E3-O's air settles at 70.00 C and the cells
   peak at 68.86 C in the 4 h; E5's air averages 58.75 C over the cycle and the cells peak at 74.73 C (MODELED).
   (I) at this corner: a cooler into the sealed case holding the cells at H1's reading takes 8.18 to 25.69 W (E3-O, COP 1.0 to 0.5) and 11.21 to 35.21 W (E5) and lifts the air to
   74.9 to 96.1 C, 4.9 to 21.1 K over the uncooled 70.00 C (E3-O) and 75.00 C (E5's 60 C dwell), onto and past the +70 C parts of OPERATING-ENVELOPE.md section 2 (the SA868,
   the AW7915-AED cards, the LimeSDR, the Xenarc) and at COP 0.5 the CM5's +85 C: INCONCLUSIVE on the input's spare power and on that cost to other functions; latent storage
   needs 0.162 L (E3-O) and 1.489 L (E5) against at most 0.121 L: rejected. Near the best corner (3.30 W/K with the other parameters favourable) 0.86 to 3.44 W of input holds the cells (3i).
   Endurance, were the cooler fed by the pack (E3-O and E5 feed it from the input): 2.52 h without it at PS-IDLE-SPEC, 2.34 to 2.47 h at the best corner's input, 1.39 to 2.12 h at
   this corner's.
   Outside FEA-008 and common to every approach: at this corner the uncooled air settles at 70.00 C in E3-O and tends to 75.00 C in E5's 60 C dwell, at or past the +70 C
   parts' limits (the SA868, the AW7915-AED cards, the LimeSDR, the Xenarc): a finding for the kit's thermal owner (section 7).

== 4. The cells, alongside the thermal measures (at most three solutions, each inside D-06's single 4S3P in the east pocket)
S1 Samsung INR18650-35E as ruled (MAKER, Ver. 1.1): the limits of section 1; min 3.35 Ah, 144.7 Wh nominal; 8 A continuous; USD 8.25 a cell (l3batt reading).
