Protection and charger changes: all three are 4.2 V a cell (the BQ25731's 16.8 V unchanged); S2 and S3 need the gauge's chemistry data for a new cell (BQ4050 image);
   S2's ambient discharge limit is the 35E's +60 C, so the ladder (OTC 44.0, OTD 57.5, UTC 1.0, UTD -9.0 C) and the hot stop stay as they are unless Samsung reads its ambient as the outside air;
   The protection and control redesign is the entry cost of any cell used above +60 C (S2 under the outside-air reading, S3): keeping H1 and H2 at their 35E-derived readings still stops
   every module in the hot margins; U2's variants are not drop-ins (MAKER, SLUSEG7D p.3): BQ7720700 OT 70 C, OVP 4.325 V, UVP 2.25 V, OV delay 1s, COUT active high 6 V; BQ7720701 OT 80 C, OVP 4.275 V, UVP 2.0 V, OV delay 1s, COUT active high 6 V; BQ7720702 OT 80 C, OVP 4.275 V, UVP 2.0 V, OV delay 4s, COUT active high 6 V; BQ7720704 OT 83 C, OVP 4.275 V, UVP 2.0 V, OV delay 1s, COUT open-drain active pulldown (DOUT active high 6 V); BQ7720705 OT 75 C, OVP 4.275 V, UVP 2.5 V, OV delay 1s, COUT active high 6 V; BQ7720706 OT 70 C, OVP 4.325 V, UVP Disabled, OV delay 2s, COUT active high 6 V;
   so the hot ladder (C1, H1, H2, OTD, SOT, U2's OT and its voltage thresholds, the PTC) and F2's replacement must be re-specified together, with their tolerance, nuisance-trip and
   permanent-trip bounds recomputed for storage and for powered operation. This record does not specify that redesign: it is the cost of entry of S2's and S3's hot rows.
Thermal-control burden: S1 none beyond the design (C1, the hot stop, the mat on input power; the coupling only for the cells, below T-H1's threshold); S2 the same; S3 the same.
   Evidence outstanding: S1 T-H1, E3-A, E3-L, E3-H, the lot's revision; S2 those plus Samsung's reading of its ambient clause and the redesign; S3 the maker's signed specification
   (none found), the maker's identity behind the marketplace listings, the redesign, the gauge data.
