== 9. U-01 BY MODE: the HL18650V class's limits established separately, the charging constraints, usable energy (the dependency round of 2 October 2026)
Classes here: MAKER (a maker's signed document or a maker's datasheet), MAKER-PAGE (a maker's product page: no signature, no test conditions), INFERRED
(computed, method stated), ASSUMPTION (a figure no held document gives), SESSION (a draft setting chosen here). No cell is adopted; every setting is a draft.

9a The limits by mode (the HL18650V's own rows: Yichun Topwell Power's product page, MAKER-PAGE, `inputs/topwell-hl18650v-page-2026-10-01.json`):
   CHARGE window              -20 to 60 C
                              condition: basis (cell surface or ambient) not stated; no state of charge; class MAKER-PAGE (headline); the signed specification must confirm: the basis, and whether the window's low end holds at every state of charge
   CHARGE, coldest row        0.1C (0.28 A a cell) to 4.1 V
                              condition: printed '-20 -10<T<=0 C': legible from -10 C; whether -20 to -10 C may charge is not legible; class MAKER-PAGE (row garbled); the signed specification must confirm: the band's lower edge, its current and voltage
   CHARGE, middle row         0.2C (0.56 A a cell) to 4.2 V
                              condition: 0 < T <= 10 C; C taken on the 2.80 Ah minimum (0.56 A = 0.2C); class MAKER-PAGE; the signed specification must confirm: the temperature basis
   CHARGE, warm row           0.5C (1.40 A a cell, the page's maximum continuous charge) to 4.2 V
                              condition: 10 < T < 60 C; no derating toward the hot end stated; class MAKER-PAGE; the signed specification must confirm: any derating or time limit at 4.2 V above 45 C
   CHARGE method and end      CC/CV to 4.2 V; termination current not stated; standard charge 0.56 A
                              condition: none stated; class MAKER-PAGE (termination absent); the signed specification must confirm: the termination current at 4.2 V and at 4.1 V
   DISCHARGE window           -40 to 85 C
                              condition: basis not stated; no current stated with it; class MAKER-PAGE (headline); the signed specification must confirm: the basis, and the current at which the ends of the window hold
   DISCHARGE end voltage      2.75 V (0 to 85 C), 2.50 V (-20 to 0 C), 2.00 V (-40 to -20 C)
                              condition: by temperature; the current not stated; class MAKER-PAGE; the signed specification must confirm: the current behind each end voltage
   DISCHARGE current          10 A continuous; pulse not stated
                              condition: no temperature or duration stated; class MAKER-PAGE (pulse absent); the signed specification must confirm: the pulse current and duration; any derating with temperature
   DISCHARGE capacity         2.90 Ah typical, 2.80 Ah minimum at 0.2C
                              condition: temperature not stated (taken as the standard condition); none at the cold end; class MAKER-PAGE (cold capacity absent); the signed specification must confirm: the capacity at -20 and -40 C at 0.2C and 0.5C to the stated end voltages
   STORAGE                    -20 to 25 C 12 months; -20 to 45 C 6 months; -40 to 60 C 3 months; -40 to 80 C within 30 days
                              condition: state of charge, recovery and self-discharge not stated; class MAKER-PAGE; the signed specification must confirm: the state of charge of each row, the recovery after it, the self-discharge rate
   REST at high charge, hot   not stated
                              condition: the kit on an input in E3-O and E5 holds the pack up to its charge; class none (not on the page); the signed specification must confirm: the recovery after E5's ten cycles and E3-O's 4 h at the kit's state of charge
   OTHER                      internal resistance at most 18 mOhm; about 44 g; at least 500 cycles (25 C, 0.5C / 1C), no end-of-life capacity
                              condition: the page's own figures, conditions as printed; class MAKER-PAGE; the signed specification must confirm: the end-of-life capacity after the stated cycles
   Comparable 18650s with makers' own sheets (context only, never a substitute for the HL18650V's figures):
   - Samsung SDI INR18650-30Q Version No. V1.0 (date of application 2020/01/17; the 30Q6 production code) (MAKER, signed specification): surface discharge -20 to 80 C (released under 60 C), ambient charge 0 to 45 C, storage 1 month -20 to 60 C at 30% of charge;
     capacity at 10 A: 60 % at -20 C, 75 % at -10 C, 80 % at 0 C, 100 % at 23 C, 95 % at 60 C; full charge stored 30 days at 60 C, recovery at least 2,320 mAh (80 % of rated).
   - Samsung SDI INR18650-30Q Version No. 1.0 (February 2015) (MAKER, signed specification): surface discharge -20 to 75 C; storage 1 month -30 to 60 C at 40±5% SOC, recovery 90 %.
   - E-One Moli Energy MOLICEL INR-18650-P28A product data sheet (MAKER, a data sheet 'for reference only', not signed: True): ambient charge 0 to 60 C, discharge -40 to 60 C; no storage clause.
   So signed sheets reach a surface discharge of +80 C, storage to -30 C and a cold discharge to -40 C; the page's rows beyond every comparable: charge below 0 C (True), storage above +60 C (True), storage below -30 C (True).
   Those rows are the ones most exposed to a narrower signed figure.

9b The charging constraints in D-06's 4S3P with the drawn charger and the pack's gauge (drafts, never applied):
   The BQ25731 has no cell temperature input (True) and ends a charge only on the host's word (True); its 4S strap is 16.800 V and BATOVP is 104 % of
   ChargeVoltage (MAKER, SLUSE66A via `review-packets/battery/CHARGER-STATE-SEQUENCE.md`). The windows are the gauge's: the BQ4050's ranges T1, T2, T5, T6, T3, T4 (True)
   set ChargingCurrent() and ChargingVoltage() per range and hold the charge FET off below UTC (MAKER, SLUUAQ3A 14.4, 2.11); the host relays them to the charger.
   Today: UTC 1.0 C (recovery 5.0 C), T1 1 C, T3 42 C, T4 43 C, OTC 44.0 C, the kit's hold below +3 C (THERMAL-COORDINATION.md section 4).
   Draft for the HL18650V class (SESSION; each threshold kept today's 1.0 K inside its band edge, as UTC sits inside the 35E's 0 C):
   CH Low Temp (T1 to T2)                            -10 to 0 C (page): 0.1C = 0.84 A for the pack, set 0.84 A; 4.10 V a cell = 16.40 V (BATOVP 17.06 V)
   CH Standard Temp low (T2 to T5)                   0 to 10 C (page): 0.2C = 1.68 A for the pack, set 1.68 A; 4.20 V a cell = 16.80 V (BATOVP 17.47 V)
   CH Recommended and Standard Temp high (T5 to T3)  10 to 60 C (page): 0.5C = 4.20 A for the pack, set 3.00 A; 4.20 V a cell = 16.80 V (BATOVP 17.47 V)
   CH thresholds: UTC -9.0 C (recovery -5.0 C), T1 -9 C, T2 1 C, T5 11 C; T3 42 C, T4 43 C and OTC 44.0 C kept (SESSION: inside the page's +60 C, for cell
      life; reversed by the signed charge rows); the kit's hold below -7 C; the gauge's CUV from 2.50 V to 2.75 V a cell (the page's end above 0 C; the
      kit's graceful line at 3.00 V under load acts first); the termination current: none on the page, TI's default 250 mA kept (ASSUMPTION).
   The drawn 3.0 A is 0.357C a cell, inside the page's 0.5C from +10 C; below it the gauge's range must lower the set current as above.
   Below the cold charge limit no charge starts (UTC holds the charge FET; the host starts none). The mat (U22 on VBAT = VSYS) warms the block first:
   on battery it is a discharge load under the cells' discharge rows, so its energy comes out of usable energy (9c); with an input and the charge FET
   off it is fed through VSYS by the source, CONDITIONAL on U-04's VSYS regulation (L4-E11). The 35E cannot feed it below UTD's -9.0 C reading
   (its discharge FET is off); the HL18650V's page lets the pack feed it down to -40 C.

